3.2. Value Proposition for AI Developers and Academics
The SSISM  MSSA Pyinnyashi system offers a rare example of ancient, culturally rich data being successfully integrated into modern computational models.
•	Data Formalization: It provides a structured \mathbf{D}, \mathbf{P}, \mathbf{H}, and \mathbf{S} data set for a historically complex system, making it accessible for Discrete Mathematics study and algorithm development.
•	Risk Analysis Model: The system can be studied as an alternative Non-Linear Predictive Model. The house progression, moving from Liability to Asset houses, mirrors common risk/reward cycles in financial or political modeling.
•	Ethical AI Context: By focusing the output on strategic advice and security warnings rather than mystical predictions, the system demonstrates how AI can be a contextual companion that respects traditional heuristics while ensuring the client's practical, real-world safety. The system’s success is validated not by prediction alone, but by the client's ability to successfully navigate the predicted environment.


